@title Quote Pricing Model Architecture
@subtitle Real-time quote pricing, Orchard Insurance
@author ML Platform
@date Reviewed 2026-10-12
@width wide

## Overview

The quote pricing service prices about 450 quotes per second at peak, with a p99 latency target of 250 ms.

## Architecture diagram

diagram ml dir=LR title="Real-time pricing topology"
ml: portal "Agent Portal" user
ml: apigw "API Gateway" lb
ml: bucket "Model Bucket" store
ml: lambda "Inference Lambda" fn focus
ml: endpoint "SageMaker Endpoint" svc focus
ml: cache "Feature Cache" cache
ml: training "Training Pipeline" svc
ml: registry "Model Registry" store
ml: portal -> apigw : quote request
ml: apigw -> lambda : invoke
ml: lambda -> cache : get features
ml: lambda -> endpoint : predict
ml: training -> registry : register model
ml: registry -> bucket : approved artifact
ml: bucket -> endpoint : load model
ml: group infvpc "Inference VPC" lambda, endpoint, cache
ml: group prod "Prod account" apigw, bucket, infvpc
ml: group mlacct "ML account" training, registry

## Capacity

table = Component,Size,Scaling; SageMaker Endpoint,ml.c6i.2xlarge,4 to 12 instances on invocations per instance; Inference Lambda,1024 MB,200 reserved concurrency; Feature Cache,cache.r7g.large,2 replicas

## Deployment

1. Register the model.
2. Approve it in Model Registry.
3. Blue/green deploy, shifting 10% of traffic every 5 minutes.
4. Roll back automatically if p99 exceeds 250 ms.

!! The Feature Cache is not a source of truth. A cache miss falls back to the policy database and adds about 90 ms.
